 lines=[f'# {sid} - TIC {tic}', '',f'Physical verdict: **{n["verdict"]}**. Bounded review: **COMPLETE**. Catalogue novelty: **{n["novelty"]}**.', '',n['finding'],'',f'Gaia selection orbit: P={float(r["gaia_period_days"]):.6f} d, {r["nss_type"]}. The edge-on conjunction approximation places the evaluated epoch at {geo["closest"]["screen_minus_pred_phase"]:+.4f} cycles from the nearest predicted conjunction; this is a conditional geometry comparison with linear covariance in lead-gaia-covariance.json, not a complete orbit fit.','', '## Source and reduction', '',f'TESScut sector {pix["sector"]}: target WCS xy=({pix["target_xy"][0]:.2f},{pix["target_xy"][1]:.2f}), deficit peak xy={pix["difference_peak_xy"]}, offset {pix["peak_to_target_pixels"]:.2f} pixel. A 3x3 sky-corrected custom aperture measures {pix["independent_aperture_depth_ppt"]:.1f} ppt on the same observing occasion ({pix["core_count"]} core and {pix["baseline_count"]} baseline cadences). There are {pix["valid_sky_pixels"]} valid positive sky pixels. Gaia capable-neighbor list is in helper-pixel-audit.json; bandpass flux ratios alone are not attribution. This independently extracts the same photons; it is not another observing occasion.','', '## Raw observations', '', '| Sector | Fitted center BTJD | Raw core deficit ppt | Fitted duration d | Local max gap d |','|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for e in sorted(m['events'],key=lambda x:x['fit_mid_btjd']):lines.append(f'| {e["sector"]} | {e["fit_mid_btjd"]:.4f} | {e["raw_core_median_deficit_ppt"]:.1f} | {e["fit_duration_days"]:.3f} | {e["local_max_gap_days"]:.3f} |')
